# Lines NoWayOS's tools/pi-run must see from the showcase on the Pi 5, in
# this order, as whole serial lines: each USB host PD's
# controller running - RP1's two, which the QEMU variant lacks - then
# systems/showcase.expect's lines as far as the Service desk's first
# session, closed with Home: the visitor sign-in twice and the Service desk
# once. A departure
# from NoWayOS's rule that a board's expect file holds every line of QEMU's:
# a board run lasts at most the watchdog's 15 s, which the script reaches
# soon after, so the rest of the Service desk, the pump and the idle paths
# are QEMU's to check (showcase.expect), the tour's (showcase-tour.expect),
# and a person's to see here, with make pi-show, which arms no watchdog. What is
# plugged into the controllers is printed between these lines and not
# checked.
# The display PD shows each frame at the monitor's own pixels.
# Each countdown tick draws its digits' slot alone: the confirmation's
# first is checked here, and any tick drawing more fails the run.
NOWAYOS: display-stub: showing each frame on the board's 1920x1080 x8r8g8b8 framebuffer at its own pixels, from row 0
NOWAYOS: usb0: starting
NOWAYOS: usb0: controller identified
NOWAYOS: usb0: halted and reset
NOWAYOS: usb0: running: a No Op command came back through DMA
NOWAYOS: usb0: ready
NOWAYOS: usb1: starting
NOWAYOS: usb1: controller identified
NOWAYOS: usb1: halted and reset
NOWAYOS: usb1: running: a No Op command came back through DMA
NOWAYOS: usb1: ready
SHOWCASE: app: starting
SHOWCASE: app: ready: a form of 4 steps and 6 fields; the idle warning after 15 s, the reset after 30 s
# The application checks in first, before the UI starts: its
# backend's stand-in answers not approved, then approves it with epoch 2,
# which every attempt's ticket carries.
SHOWCASE: app: checking in: 1
SHOWCASE: app: check-in 1: not approved; awaiting approval, code 3FA1 075C E219 8840
SHOWCASE: app: checking in: 2
SHOWCASE: app: check-in 2: approved, epoch 2; in service
SHOWCASE: ui: starting
SHOWCASE: ui: the display is 1920x1080 Xrgb8888 at scale 2
SHOWCASE: ui: showing launcher
SHOWCASE: ui: theme launcher
SHOWCASE: ui: action Visitor sign-in
SHOWCASE: ui: showing welcome
SHOWCASE: ui: theme Orrinvale
SHOWCASE: ui: action Sign in as a visitor
SHOWCASE: ui: showing about-you
SHOWCASE: ui: action Next
SHOWCASE: ui: showing visiting
SHOWCASE: ui: action Next
SHOWCASE: ui: showing purpose
SHOWCASE: ui: action Next
SHOWCASE: ui: showing site-rules
SHOWCASE: ui: action Next
SHOWCASE: ui: showing check
SHOWCASE: ui: action Sign in
SHOWCASE: visitor: the service stand-in will accept attempt 1 (epoch 2)
SHOWCASE: ui: showing signing-in
SHOWCASE: visitor: the service stand-in accepts attempt 1
SHOWCASE: visitor: session 1 ended: submitted
SHOWCASE: ui: showing signed-in
SHOWCASE: ui: seconds left: 10
SHOWCASE: ui: seconds left: 9
SHOWCASE: ui: countdown drawn alone: 61x47 px of the 1920x1080 screen
SHOWCASE: ui: action Done
SHOWCASE: ui: showing launcher
SHOWCASE: ui: theme launcher
SHOWCASE: ui: action Visitor sign-in
SHOWCASE: ui: showing welcome
SHOWCASE: ui: action Sign in as a visitor
SHOWCASE: ui: showing about-you
SHOWCASE: ui: action Next
SHOWCASE: ui: showing visiting
SHOWCASE: ui: action Next
SHOWCASE: ui: showing purpose
SHOWCASE: ui: action Next
SHOWCASE: ui: showing site-rules
SHOWCASE: ui: action Next
SHOWCASE: ui: showing check
SHOWCASE: ui: action Demo: service down
SHOWCASE: visitor: demo: the service is down for this session, as the person asked
SHOWCASE: visitor: the service stand-in will fail attempt 1 (epoch 2)
SHOWCASE: ui: showing signing-in
SHOWCASE: visitor: the service stand-in fails attempt 1: the service is down
SHOWCASE: ui: showing not-signed-in
SHOWCASE: ui: action Finish
SHOWCASE: visitor: session 2 ended: cancelled
SHOWCASE: ui: showing launcher
SHOWCASE: ui: action Service desk
SHOWCASE: ui: showing welcome
SHOWCASE: ui: theme Service desk
SHOWCASE: ui: action Start
SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-text
SHOWCASE: ui: action Home
SHOWCASE: ui: showing launcher
SHOWCASE: app: session 1 ended: abandoned by the UI

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# a fault reported by the Microkit monitor, a kernel error message, a panic, a
# PD giving up, a record refused or rejected, a screen that could not be
# shown, a session ended for a fault, input or an action dropped anywhere -
# by the UART input PD, at the broker's rate, for want of room in the UI's
# ring or in the ring to the application.
!cannot show frames
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!fan: no temperature
!PWM1 is not counting
!refused
!rejected
!could not be shown
!ended: a fault
!out of service
!dropped so far
!over its rate
!the UI's ring is full
# A countdown's tick that drew more than its digits' slot.
!countdown drawn with more

# Nothing derived from what was typed: no frame's or scan-out hash,
# which the display PD prints only when it is not quiet, and nothing the
# script types - every name starts zqvj, the reference is 9081726354.
# tools/check-quiet requires the hash line, and each text typed to start
# with a text forbidden here.
!display-stub: frame
!zqvj
!9081726354
